  <div class="card" id="1">
    <h2><span>📋</span> 1. Information We Collect - What Data Do We Collect?</h2>
    <p>When you use <b>LearnHTMLCSSJS.com</b> to learn HTML, learn CSS, and learn JavaScript, we collect only the minimum information needed to make your learning experience better. We collect two types of information: information you give us directly, and information collected automatically.</p>
    <p><b>A) Information You Provide:</b> When you create a free account on our website, we collect your <b>name, username, email address, and password</b>. Your password is stored in encrypted form using bcrypt hashing, so even we cannot see your real password. When you complete lessons and tests, we save your <b>test scores, total marks, progress, and ranking</b> to show on your dashboard. When you use our Contact Us page, we collect your <b>name, email, topic, and message</b> so we can reply to you. We never ask for your CNIC, bank account, credit card, or any sensitive financial information. Our course is 100% free, so we never ask for payment details.</p>
    <p><b>B) Information Collected Automatically:</b> When you visit our website, we may automatically collect your <b>IP address, browser type, device type, operating system, pages visited, time spent on each lesson, and how you found our website</b> - for example, from Google search, YouTube, Facebook, or WhatsApp. This helps us understand which lessons are most popular, like Lesson 1 - What is HTML, Lesson 11 - What is CSS, Lesson 21 - What is JavaScript, and Lesson 48 - Freelancing Guide, and improve them. This data is anonymous and cannot identify you personally.</p>
    <div class="highlight green"><b>✅ We Never Sell Your Data:</b> We do NOT sell, rent, or share your personal information with anyone for marketing. Your email will never be sold to third parties.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" id="2">
    <h2><span>🎯</span> 2. How We Use Your Information - Why Do We Need It?</h2>
    <p>We use your information only for the following purposes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>To Provide The Course:</b> To create your account, save your lesson progress, show your dashboard, calculate your total marks, and show your name on the ranking page.</li>
      <li><b>To Improve Learning:</b> To understand which HTML, CSS, and JavaScript lessons students find difficult, so we can make them simpler and add more examples.</li>
      <li><b>To Send Important Emails:</b> To reply to your contact messages, send password reset links, and inform you about new lessons, new tests, and certificates.</li>
      <li><b>To Keep Website Secure:</b> To prevent fake accounts, cheating in tests, hacking, and spam. To protect our students and website.</li>
      <li><b>To Show Relevant Content:</b> To show you lessons and projects that match your level - beginner, intermediate, or advanced.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We will never use your email to send spam. We send only important emails related to your learning. You can ask us anytime to stop sending emails by contacting us at <a href="mailto:contact@learnhtmlcssjs.com">contact@learnhtmlcssjs.com</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card" id="3">
    <h2><span>🍪</span> 3. Cookies Policy - What Are Cookies?</h2>
    <p>Cookies are small text files stored on your device when you visit a website. <b>LearnHTMLCSSJS.com</b> uses cookies to keep you logged in, remember your progress, and understand how students use our website. We use two types of cookies. <b>Essential Cookies:</b> These are required for login, session, and security. Without them, you cannot stay logged in or save your test scores. <b>Analytics Cookies:</b> These help us count how many students visited our website, which pages are popular, and how long students spend learning. This data is anonymous. You can delete or block cookies from your browser settings at any time. If you block essential cookies, some features like login and dashboard may not work correctly. By continuing to use our website, you agree to our use of cookies.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card" id="4">
    <h2><span>📊</span> 4. Google Analytics, Google AdSense & Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>Our website may use <b>Google Analytics</b> to understand website traffic and <b>Google AdSense</b> to show ads and keep our course free forever. Google may use cookies to show ads based on your interests and previous visits. You can control personalized ads by visiting Google Ad Settings. We may also use <b>MongoDB Atlas</b> to securely store your account data, and <b>Cloud Hosting</b> services like Render, Vercel, or Netlify to host our website. These services have their own privacy policies and follow strict data protection rules. We do not control third-party websites. If you click on an external link, for example to Fiverr, Upwork, YouTube, or GitHub, that website's privacy policy will apply. We recommend reading their policies before sharing your information.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card" id="5">
    <h2><span>🔒</span> 5. Data Security - How Do We Protect Your Data?</h2>
    <p>We take your security very seriously. Your password is hashed with <b>bcrypt</b> and never stored in plain text. Your login session uses secure <b>JWT tokens and HTTP-only cookies</b>. Your data is stored on secure servers with limited access. Only our website admin can access user data for support and maintenance. However, no method of transmission over the internet is 100% secure. While we do our best to protect your information, we cannot guarantee absolute security. We advise you to use a strong password, never share your password with anyone, and log out when using a shared computer or mobile phone in a school, college, or internet cafe.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card" id="6">
    <h2><span>🔗</span> 6. Third-Party Links, Embeds & External Websites</h2>
    <p>Our lessons may contain links to external websites like <b>W3Schools, MDN Web Docs, CodePen, GitHub, Fiverr, Upwork, and YouTube</b> for extra learning. These websites are not operated by us. We are not responsible for their content or privacy practices. When you leave our website, we encourage you to review the privacy policy of every website you visit. Our free web development course is designed to help you learn HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, and external resources are provided only for your benefit and extra practice.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card" id="7">
    <h2><span>👶</span> 7. Children's Privacy - Students Under 13</h2>
    <p>Our website is designed for students of all ages, including school students from Class 6 and above who want to learn coding. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13 without parental consent. If you are under 13, please ask your parent or teacher before creating an account. If a parent believes their child has provided personal information to us, please contact us at <a href="mailto:contact@learnhtmlcssjs.com">contact@learnhtmlcssjs.com</a> and we will delete that information immediately. We believe coding should be safe for every student in Pakistan, India, Bangladesh, and all over the world.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card" id="8">
    <h2><span>⚖️</span> 8. Your Rights - You Control Your Data</h2>
    <p>You have full control over your data. You have the right to:</p>
